# fallpause: recorded by the port from this script (no cheats, so format 4, which DOS
# replays), from the saved game fallrestore writes; its golden is DOS's replay of that
# recording. "Journey Onward" and slot I (the player on the platform at (9,6), facing north);
# Shift+D, 45 degrees; s held a second, which walks north-east off the platform's edge at the
# walking speed, 352, so 248 on each axis (a player under 3/10 of the run speed stops at a
# ledge instead); then the restore prompt opened and cancelled (Ctrl+R, Escape) four times
# while the player falls. The first step after each prompt is check_physics's 40h units, a
# whole step, and zspeed is the fall over the slow axis (vel2 * 256 / 248), 1222 at the
# second prompt, so MOTION.C's full_move shifts it out of 16 bits: in DOS the step comes out
# upwards and full_move takes it for a landing (do_zbounce) in mid-air, where the port before
# its fix moved the player down
9000 key esc
12000 key enter        # Journey Onward
15000 key enter        # slot I
25000 down shift       # Shift+D: 45 degrees right
25050 key d
25100 up shift
27000 down s           # walk
28000 up s
28200 down ctrl        # the restore prompt, cancelled, four times
28250 key r
28300 up ctrl
28600 key esc
28750 down ctrl
28800 key r
28850 up ctrl
29150 key esc
29300 down ctrl
29350 key r
29400 up ctrl
29700 key esc
29850 down ctrl
29900 key r
29950 up ctrl
30250 key esc
